# Equinox counts only the lands Cleansing would really destroy (CR 701.19a; the owner's decision of 2026-11-28): Bot1
# controls two Plains and Dryad Arbor, which Death Ward has given a regeneration shield, and each player has 1 life. With
# no life paid, Cleansing would destroy the two Plains and the Arbor would regenerate, and two is no more than the 2 life
# the players could pay for them, so sparing every land it would destroy is a choice they may make: it is not countered
# (rulings). Then no one pays: the Plains are destroyed, and the Arbor regenerates, tapped.

[Life]
Bot1: 1
Bot2: 1

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Equinox
Dryad Arbor
Death Ward
Plains
Plains
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Cleansing
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Equinox.Cast(Plains)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Dryad Arbor.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot2.Hand.Cleansing.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Death Ward.Cast(Dryad Arbor)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate(Stack.Cleansing; Ability: Counter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Choose()
Bot1.Choose()

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Dryad Arbor; Mox Pearl
Bot1.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Tapped = true
Bot1.Life = 1
Bot2.Life = 1
